Package: unpakt
Version: @VERSION@-1
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: krotrn <krotrn.ks@gmail.com>
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Recommends: libfuse2t64 | libfuse2
Homepage: https://github.com/krotrn/unpakt
Description: Install, update and roll back portable apps and packages per user
 unpakt installs AppImages, tarballs and deb, rpm and pacman packages into
 your home directory, adds launcher entries and a command on PATH, and can
 update or roll back each app. Packages are unpacked, never run, and checked
 first for whether they will work on this system. It comes with a command line tool (unpakt) and a GTK 4 / libadwaita
 interface (unpakt-gui).
 .
 Running AppImages directly needs FUSE 2; without it unpakt extracts them.
